window.AG_PRACTICE["zangfu"] = {"id":"zangfu","axis":"theory","seal":"理","scene":"art/scene-hall.jpg","title":"Zang-Fu Match","titleZh":"臟腑配對","sub":"What each organ governs, opens into, and pairs with","subZh":"各臟所主、所開之竅、所配之腑","mentor":{"key":"shu","nm":"Shū Chī","nmZh":"書癡","line":"\"Students memorise the organs as a list. A list is useless. Learn what each one *does*, and the symptoms will sort themselves.\"","lineZh":"「學生把臟腑背成一張名單。名單沒有用。要記它做什麼事，症狀自己就會歸位。」"},"card":{"h":"Organs Are Functions 臟腑者，功能也","hZh":"","p":"In TCM an organ is defined by what it governs, not by where it sits. The Spleen is not a location — it is transformation, ascent of the clear, and holding blood in the vessels. Read a symptom, ask which function has failed, and the organ names itself.","pZh":"中醫之臟腑，以功能立名，不以形質定位。脾非一處，乃運化、升清、統血也。見一症，先問何功能失職，其臟自明。"},"items":[{"k":"match","q":"Match each zang organ to its paired fu organ (interior-exterior).","qZh":"五臟配六腑（臟腑表裡）。","pairs":[{"l":"Heart","lZh":"心","r":"Small Intestine","rZh":"小腸"},{"l":"Lung","lZh":"肺","r":"Large Intestine","rZh":"大腸"},{"l":"Spleen","lZh":"脾","r":"Stomach","rZh":"胃"},{"l":"Liver","lZh":"肝","r":"Gallbladder","rZh":"膽"},{"l":"Kidney","lZh":"腎","r":"Bladder","rZh":"膀胱"}],"note":"Interior-exterior pairs share a channel connection, so one can be treated through the other. The Lung-Large Intestine pair explains why constipation can follow a Lung pattern, and why LI4 helps a cough. 表裡相配者，經脈相互絡屬，故可互治。肺與大腸相表裡，故肺病可見便秘，合谷亦可治咳。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which pair is missing from the classic five, making six?","qZh":"五臟之外，尚有一對，合為六，是何？","opts":[{"t":"Pericardium and San Jiao","c":"心包與三焦","ok":1,"note":"The Pericardium 心包 shields the Heart and the San Jiao 三焦 is the passage for qi and water through the three burners. They complete the twelve channels. 心包護心，三焦為氣與水之通道，主持諸氣、通調水道。二者足成十二經。"},{"t":"Brain and Marrow","c":"腦與髓","ok":0,"note":"Those belong to the Extraordinary Fu 奇恆之腑, which store like zang but are shaped like fu. They are not part of the twelve channels. 此屬奇恆之腑：形如腑而藏如臟，不入十二經。"},{"t":"Uterus and Bladder","c":"胞宮與膀胱","ok":0,"note":"The Bladder is already paired with the Kidney, and the Uterus is an Extraordinary Fu. 膀胱已配腎，胞宮屬奇恆之腑。"},{"t":"Diaphragm and Chest","c":"膈與胸","ok":0,"note":"Anatomical regions, not organs in the zang-fu system. 此為部位，非臟腑之名。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which organ governs transformation and transportation, and holds blood in the vessels?","qZh":"何臟主運化，又主統血？","opts":[{"t":"Spleen","c":"脾","ok":1,"note":"Three functions to remember together: transform and transport food into qi and blood 運化, raise the clear 升清, and hold blood inside the vessels 統血. Bruising easily, prolapse and loose stool all trace back here. 脾三功並記：運化水穀、升清、統血。易瘀斑、內臟下垂、便溏，皆由此出。"},{"t":"Stomach","c":"胃","ok":0,"note":"The Stomach receives and ripens 受納腐熟 and its qi descends. It is the Spleen's partner, not its replacement. 胃主受納腐熟，其氣以降為順。與脾相配，非其替。"},{"t":"Liver","c":"肝","ok":0,"note":"The Liver stores blood 藏血 and spreads qi 疏泄 — it holds a reserve, but it does not keep blood inside the vessel walls. 肝藏血、主疏泄。藏者，貯也；統者，攝也。二者不同。"},{"t":"Heart","c":"心","ok":0,"note":"The Heart governs the blood vessels and houses the spirit — it moves blood, it does not manufacture or contain it. 心主血脈、藏神。行血而非生血、攝血。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each organ to the tissue it governs.","qZh":"五臟配五體。","pairs":[{"l":"Liver","lZh":"肝","r":"Sinews","rZh":"筋"},{"l":"Heart","lZh":"心","r":"Vessels","rZh":"脈"},{"l":"Spleen","lZh":"脾","r":"Flesh and limbs","rZh":"肌肉四肢"},{"l":"Lung","lZh":"肺","r":"Skin and body hair","rZh":"皮毛"},{"l":"Kidney","lZh":"腎","r":"Bones","rZh":"骨"}],"note":"This is why cramps and stiff tendons send you to the Liver, why weak limbs and heavy flesh send you to the Spleen, and why bone and low-back complaints in an older patient send you to the Kidney. 故拘攣筋強當察肝，四肢無力、肌肉消瘦當察脾，年高骨弱腰痛當察腎。"},{"k":"match","q":"Match each organ to the fluid it produces.","qZh":"五臟配五液。","pairs":[{"l":"Heart","lZh":"心","r":"Sweat","rZh":"汗"},{"l":"Lung","lZh":"肺","r":"Nasal mucus","rZh":"涕"},{"l":"Spleen","lZh":"脾","r":"Drool","rZh":"涎"},{"l":"Liver","lZh":"肝","r":"Tears","rZh":"淚"},{"l":"Kidney","lZh":"腎","r":"Spittle","rZh":"唾"}],"note":"Sweat and blood share a source, which is why heavy sweating injures the Heart and heart-blood loss dries the sweat. Dry eyes point at Liver blood; a dry nose at Lung yin. 汗血同源，故大汗傷心，心血虛則汗少。目乾當責肝血，鼻乾當責肺陰。"},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient is short of breath, sweats during the day and catches every cold. Which organ's qi is weak?","qZh":"氣短、日間自汗、易感冒，何臟氣虛？","opts":[{"t":"Lung","c":"肺","ok":1,"note":"The Lung governs qi and controls the exterior through wei qi. When Lung qi is weak the surface is not defended: spontaneous daytime sweating, breathlessness on exertion, and repeated colds. 肺主氣，外合皮毛，衛外而為固。肺氣虛則表不固：自汗、動則氣短、屢感風邪。"},{"t":"Kidney","c":"腎","ok":0,"note":"Kidney qi failing to grasp qi 腎不納氣 gives breathlessness that is worse on inhalation and worse with exertion, usually in long illness — plus low back and urinary signs. Not the first answer for a simple weak exterior. 腎不納氣者，呼多吸少、動則喘甚，多見於久病，且兼腰膝、小便之症。非表虛之首選。"},{"t":"Heart","c":"心","ok":0,"note":"Heart qi deficiency brings palpitations and breathlessness, but with chest symptoms and a weak or irregular pulse — not a poorly defended exterior. 心氣虛見心悸氣短，然兼胸中之症、脈弱或結代，非表衛不固。"},{"t":"Liver","c":"肝","ok":0,"note":"The Liver does not govern the exterior or the breath. 肝不主表，亦不主呼吸。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which statement distinguishes zang from fu?","qZh":"臟與腑之別，何說為是？","opts":[{"t":"Zang store and do not drain; fu transmit and do not store","c":"臟藏精氣而不瀉，腑傳化物而不藏","ok":1,"note":"The classical line, and it is practical: zang patterns are usually deficiency, fu patterns are usually excess and blockage. A blocked bowel is a fu problem; an empty Kidney is a zang problem. 此《素問》之語，亦切於用：臟病多虛，腑病多實多滯。腑不通者病在腑，腎精虧者病在臟。"},{"t":"Zang are solid, fu are hollow, and nothing follows from it","c":"臟實腑空，此外無他義","ok":0,"note":"The shape is real but it is only half the statement. What matters clinically is the difference in function — storing versus passing through. 形質之別誠有，然僅其半。臨床之要在功能：藏與傳化之異。"},{"t":"Zang are yin organs and fu are unimportant","c":"臟為陰，腑無足輕重","ok":0,"note":"Zang are yin and fu are yang, but the fu are not secondary — most acute illness passes through them. 臟屬陰、腑屬陽，然腑非次要，急病多由腑而行。"},{"t":"Fu store essence and zang move waste","c":"腑藏精，臟傳化","ok":0,"note":"Reversed. Zang store, fu transmit. 顛倒矣。臟藏而腑傳。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which organ is called the residence of the spirit, and shows itself in the complexion?","qZh":"何臟藏神，其華在面？","opts":[{"t":"Heart","c":"心","ok":1,"note":"The Heart governs blood and vessels, houses the spirit 藏神, opens into the tongue, and its bloom is on the face — which is why a pale or dull complexion and disturbed sleep are read together. 心主血脈、藏神、開竅於舌、其華在面。故面色與睡眠常並讀。"},{"t":"Liver","c":"肝","ok":0,"note":"The Liver's bloom is in the nails, and it houses the hun 魂 rather than the shen. 肝其華在爪，所藏者魂而非神。"},{"t":"Kidney","c":"腎","ok":0,"note":"The Kidney's bloom is in the hair of the head, and it stores essence and will 志. 腎其華在髮，藏精藏志。"},{"t":"Spleen","c":"脾","ok":0,"note":"The Spleen's bloom is on the lips, and it houses thought 意. 脾其華在唇，藏意。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each organ to where its bloom shows.","qZh":"五臟配其華。","pairs":[{"l":"Heart","lZh":"心","r":"Face","rZh":"面"},{"l":"Liver","lZh":"肝","r":"Nails","rZh":"爪"},{"l":"Spleen","lZh":"脾","r":"Lips","rZh":"唇"},{"l":"Lung","lZh":"肺","r":"Body hair","rZh":"毛"},{"l":"Kidney","lZh":"腎","r":"Head hair","rZh":"髮"}],"note":"The bloom 華 is where an organ's surplus shows on the outside. Brittle ridged nails point at Liver blood; hair thinning early in life points at Kidney essence. 華者，臟氣之餘見於外也。爪脆有稜當責肝血，早年髮落當責腎精。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which function does the Liver's 疏泄 (free coursing) NOT include?","qZh":"下列何者非肝主疏泄之所司？","opts":[{"t":"Grasping qi on inhalation","c":"納氣","ok":1,"note":"Grasping qi belongs to the Kidney. Free coursing covers the smooth flow of qi, emotional ease, digestion via bile and the Spleen's ascent, and the regularity of the menses. 納氣屬腎。疏泄所司者：氣機調暢、情志舒達、助脾胃運化與膽汁疏泄、調暢月經。"},{"t":"Smooth flow of qi through the body","c":"調暢氣機","ok":0,"note":"This is the core of free coursing. 此正疏泄之本義。"},{"t":"Emotional ease","c":"調暢情志","ok":0,"note":"Constrained Liver qi is the commonest cause of a sighing, irritable, tight-chested presentation. 肝鬱者常見善太息、煩躁、胸脅悶。"},{"t":"Helping the Spleen and Stomach transform food","c":"助脾胃運化","ok":0,"note":"When the Liver fails to course, it invades the Spleen — belching, rib-side fullness and loose stool with emotional triggers. 肝失疏泄則橫逆犯脾：噯氣、脅脹、遇情志而便溏。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which organ opens into both the ears and the two lower orifices?","qZh":"何臟開竅於耳及二陰？","opts":[{"t":"Kidney","c":"腎","ok":1,"note":"The Kidney stores essence, governs water and the bones, produces marrow, grasps qi, and opens into the ears and the two lower orifices — which is why tinnitus, nocturia and dawn diarrhoea can all belong to one organ. 腎藏精、主水、主骨生髓、主納氣，開竅於耳及二陰。故耳鳴、夜尿、五更瀉可同屬一臟。"},{"t":"Liver","c":"肝","ok":0,"note":"The Liver opens into the eyes. 肝開竅於目。"},{"t":"Spleen","c":"脾","ok":0,"note":"The Spleen opens into the mouth. 脾開竅於口。"},{"t":"Lung","c":"肺","ok":0,"note":"The Lung opens into the nose. 肺開竅於鼻。"}]}]};
